@startuml D02-multi-task-race
!theme plain
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.5

title D-02 — Multi-Task Race Condition\nTwo facilities simultaneously accept the same referral

actor "Initiating\nFacility" as initiator   #FFF9C4
actor "Facility A" as facilityA             #BBDEFB
actor "Facility B" as facilityB             #C8E6C9
database "FHIR Server" as server            #E3F2FD
actor "Patient" as patient                  #F3E5F5

autonumber

initiator -> server : POST ServiceRequest (status=active) → SR/obs-002
initiator -> server : POST Task (status=requested, focus=SR/obs-002) → Task/req-001

note over initiator
  Notification broadcast (out-of-band)
  to both Facility A and Facility B
  (no routing mechanism defined in IG)
end note

facilityA -> server : POST Task\n(status=accepted\n owner=Org/facility-a\n focus=SR/obs-002) → Task/acc-001
facilityB -> server : POST Task\n(status=accepted\n owner=Org/facility-b\n focus=SR/obs-002) → Task/acc-002

note over server #FFCCCC
  Server accepts both POSTs.
  No uniqueness constraint on Task.focus.
  No "one active Task per ServiceRequest" rule.
end note

facilityA -> patient : "Come to Facility A at 2pm."
facilityB -> patient : "Come to Facility B at 3pm."

note over patient #FFCCCC
  Patient receives contradictory instructions.
  Both appointments were created from the same referral.
end note

facilityA -> server : GET Task?focus=SR/obs-002
server --> facilityA : Task/req-001, Task/acc-001, **Task/acc-002**
note over facilityA : "Who is Task/acc-002?\n   Facility A discovers\n   the conflict only by\n   actively querying."

note right of server
  Final state:
  SR/obs-002:   status=active
  Task/req-001: status=requested (never updated)
  Task/acc-001: status=accepted, owner=Facility A
  Task/acc-002: status=accepted, owner=Facility B

  No profile constraint was violated.
  No resolution mechanism is defined.
  Who cancels which Task?
  Who notifies the patient?
  The IG is silent.
end note

@enduml
